# The public landing is the site root (index.html), so `/` itself needs no
# rule: it is served directly. Worker static assets serve 404.html for
# unknown paths via wrangler.toml.
# These two rules only exist for back-compat, so old bookmarks, shared links
# and any external reference to the former /site/ path still land on the app.
# `site/index.html` is also kept in the repo as a meta-refresh stub, which
# covers deployments where `_redirects` is not applied.
# A wildcard redirect would also match its destination and create a loop.
/site/ / 301
/site/index.html / 301
